{
  "format": "bgsim.model",
  "language": "0.1.0",
  "name": "hydraulic-circuit",
  "$comment": "A small open-loop hydraulic circuit from the hydraulic component library: an electric motor (SpeedSource, 150 rad/s) drives a 10 cm^3/rev FixedDisplacementPump from the tank; a PressureReliefValve (100 bar) protects the pump line, a CheckValve feeds the rail, and a 2 m hose (Pipe, 2 segments) connects the rail to a 0.2 l Accumulator (50 bar precharge). A 4/3 DirectionalValve43 (2% overlap) driven by a sine spool command extends a HydraulicCylinder with a 100 kg load and a 2000 N*s/m damper from 0.5 s to 1.5 s and retracts it from 1.5 s to 2.5 s.",
